   "source": [
    "# Benchmark: VLM (LLaVA) vs LLM (Claude) vs Geometric Extraction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Obiettivo**: Confrontare tre metodi di estrazione prodotti da scontrini:\n",
    "1. **Geometrico**: estrai dalla posizione dei prezzi (locale, gratis)\n",
    "2. **Claude LLM**: OCR testo → Claude estrae (pagato, €0.01-0.02/scontrino)\n",
    "3. **LLaVA VLM**: foto direttamente → LLaVA estrae (Kaggle GPU, gratis)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Metriche dichiarate PRIMA di misurare**:\n",
    "- **Principale**: numero di items estratti correttamente (nome + prezzo)\n",
    "- **Di guardia 1**: accuracy dei nomi (match con baseline geometrico)\n",
    "- **Di guardia 2**: accuracy dei prezzi\n",
    "- **Di guardia 3**: tempo di estrazione per scontrino\n",
    "- **Di guardia 4**: costi (API calls, GPU hours)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset**: 50 scontrini random dal dataset ticket-tracer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Kaggle setup\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import time\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from collections import defaultdict\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Imports OK\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check GPU\n",
    "!nvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,memory.total --format=csv,noheader"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Parte 1: Carica Dataset (50 Scontrini Random)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download dataset da GitHub (o monta da locale se su Kaggle)\n",
    "# Per ora, simula 50 scontrini con OCR grezzo\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fake OCR texts (esempi reali dal dataset)\n",
    "sample_ocr_texts = [\n",
    "    \"\"\"CONSUM\n",
    "PANET 11 UN 2.55\n",
    "LLET SEN.CONSUM 1L 1.23\n",
    "TOTAL 3.78\"\"\",\n",
    "    \"\"\"CHART\n",
    "IOGURT CABRA 2.08\n",
    "FORMATGE BRIE 3.45\n",
    "TOTAL 5.53\"\"\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# TODO: Carica 50 file reali da data/estratti/*.json\n",
    "print(f\"Campione OCR testi: {len(sample_ocr_texts)}\")\n",
    "for i, text in enumerate(sample_ocr_texts[:2]):\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nSample {i}:\")\n",
    "    print(text[:100] + \"...\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Parte 2: Metodo 1 - Geometric Extraction (Baseline)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Simula estrazione geometrica (come in fase_c_geometrica.py)\n",
    "def extract_geometric(ocr_text):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Simula estrazione geometrica:\n",
    "    - Trova righe con prezzi (regex \\d+[.,]\\d{2})\n",
    "    - Associa nome dalla sinistra\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    import re\n",
    "    \n",
    "    items = []\n",
    "    lines = ocr_text.strip().split('\\n')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for line in lines:\n",
    "        # Regex: trova prezzo\n",
    "        match = re.search(r'(\\d+[.,]\\d{2})$', line.strip())\n",
    "        if match:\n",
    "            price = match.group(1).replace(',', '.')\n",
    "            name = line[:match.start()].strip()\n",
    "            if name:\n",
    "                items.append({'name': name, 'price': float(price), 'method': 'geometric'})\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {'items': items, 'success': len(items) > 0}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test\nresult_geo = extract_geometric(sample_ocr_texts[0])\nprint(f\"Geometric extraction result: {result_geo}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Parte 3: Metodo 2 - Claude LLM (via API)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Claude LLM extraction\n",
    "# NOTA: richiede ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in env\n",
    "\n",
    "def extract_claude_llm(ocr_text):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Chiama Claude API per estrarre prodotti da testo OCR.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    import anthropic\n",
    "    \n",
    "    api_key = os.environ.get('ANTHROPIC_API_KEY')\n",
    "    if not api_key:\n",
    "        print(\"⚠️  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY not set, skipping Claude test\")\n",
    "        return {'items': [], 'success': False, 'error': 'no_api_key'}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    client = anthropic.Anthropic(api_key=api_key)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    prompt = f\"\"\"Estrai i prodotti da questo testo OCR da uno scontrino.\n",
    "Per ogni prodotto, dammi NOME e PREZZO in formato JSON.\n",
    "\n",
    "Testo OCR:\n{ocr_text}\n\n\nRispondi con JSON: [{{'name': '...', 'price': X.XX}}]\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        response = client.messages.create(\n",
    "            model=\"claude-3-haiku-20240307\",  # economico per test\n",
    "            max_tokens=500,\n",
    "            messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}]\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Parse response\n",
    "        text = response.content[0].text\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Extract JSON\n",
    "        import re\n",
    "        json_match = re.search(r'\\[.*\\]', text, re.DOTALL)\n",
    "        if json_match:\n",
    "            items = json.loads(json_match.group())\n",
    "            for item in items:\n",
    "                item['method'] = 'claude'\n",
    "            return {'items': items, 'success': True}\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        return {'items': [], 'success': False, 'error': str(e)}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {'items': [], 'success': False}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Claude LLM extractor ready (requires API key)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Parte 4: Metodo 3 - LLaVA VLM (Kaggle GPU)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install LLaVA\n",
    "!pip install -q git+https://github.com/haotian-liu/LLaVA.git\n",
    "!pip install -q transformers pillow torch\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ LLaVA installed\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load LLaVA model (once)\n",
    "from transformers import AutoProcessor, LlavaForConditionalGeneration\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use smaller model for faster inference\n",
    "model_id = \"llava-hf/llava-1.5-7b-hf\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Loading LLaVA model (first time, takes ~2-3 min)...\")\n",
    "processor = AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(model_id)\n",
    "model = LlavaForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    model_id,\n",
    "    torch_dtype=torch.float16,\n",
    "    device_map=\"auto\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ LLaVA model loaded\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def extract_llava_vlm(image_path):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Chiama LLaVA per estrarre prodotti direttamente da immagine.\n    \"\"\"\n",
    "    from PIL import Image\n",
    "    import torch\n",
    "    import json\n",
    "    import re\n",
    "    \n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        # Load image\n",
    "        image = Image.open(image_path).convert('RGB')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Prepare inputs\n",
    "        prompt = \"\"\"Estrai i prodotti da questo scontrino.\n",
    "Per ogni prodotto dammi NOME e PREZZO.\n",
    "Rispondi in JSON: [{\"name\": \"...\", \"price\": X.XX}]\"\"\"\n",
    "        \n",
    "        inputs = processor(prompt, image, return_tensors='pt').to(model.device, torch.float16)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Generate\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=300)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Decode\n",
    "        text = processor.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Extract JSON\n",
    "        json_match = re.search(r'\\[.*\\]', text, re.DOTALL)\n",
    "        if json_match:\n",
    "            items = json.loads(json_match.group())\n",
    "            for item in items:\n",
    "                item['method'] = 'llava'\n",
    "            return {'items': items, 'success': True}\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        return {'items': [], 'success': False, 'error': str(e)}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {'items': [], 'success': False}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"LLaVA VLM extractor ready\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Parte 5: Benchmark Compare"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Metrics\n",
    "results = {\n",
    "    'geometric': [],\n",
    "    'claude': [],\n",
    "    'llava': []\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "times = {\n",
    "    'geometric': [],\n",
    "    'claude': [],\n",
    "    'llava': []\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test on samples\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== BENCHMARK START ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTesting on {len(sample_ocr_texts)} samples...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for idx, ocr_text in enumerate(sample_ocr_texts):\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n--- Sample {idx} ---\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Geometric\n",
    "    t0 = time.time()\n",
    "    result_geo = extract_geometric(ocr_text)\n",
    "    t_geo = time.time() - t0\n",
    "    results['geometric'].append(result_geo)\n",
    "    times['geometric'].append(t_geo)\n",
    "    print(f\"Geometric: {len(result_geo['items'])} items, {t_geo:.3f}s\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Claude (skipped if no API key)\n",
    "    if os.environ.get('ANTHROPIC_API_KEY'):\n",
    "        t0 = time.time()\n",
    "        result_claude = extract_claude_llm(ocr_text)\n",
    "        t_claude = time.time() - t0\n",
    "        results['claude'].append(result_claude)\n",
    "        times['claude'].append(t_claude)\n",
    "        print(f\"Claude: {len(result_claude['items'])} items, {t_claude:.3f}s\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # LLaVA (skipped if no image)\n",
    "    # TODO: se hai la foto, testala\n",
    "    print(f\"LLaVA: (needs image file, skipped for now)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== BENCHMARK END ===\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Parte 6: Risultati e Confronto"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Summary stats\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== SUMMARY ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for method in ['geometric', 'claude', 'llava']:\n",
    "    if results[method]:\n",
    "        successful = sum(1 for r in results[method] if r.get('success'))\n",
    "        total_items = sum(len(r.get('items', [])) for r in results[method])\n",
    "        avg_time = np.mean(times[method]) if times[method] else 0\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(f\"\\n{method.upper()}:\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Success rate: {successful}/{len(results[method])} ({100*successful//len(results[method])}%)\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Total items extracted: {total_items}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Avg time per scontrino: {avg_time:.3f}s\")\n    else:
    "        print(f\"\\n{method.upper()}: (skipped)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Costs (estimated)\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== COSTS (Estimated for 200 scontrini/giorno) ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Geometric: €0 (local, no API)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Claude: €200 × €0.02 = €4/day = €120/month\")\n",
    "print(f\"LLaVA: €0 (Kaggle GPU free, limited to 30h/week)\")"
   ]
